# Answer key for B9 t1_breadth.sql - names and resolution, breadth.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# Conventions: all of B1-B4, plus D-23..D-25 (decided 2026-10-03, not implemented).
# Every node is schema-qualified (D-25). A forbid applies to the whole file, so a fact that
# is right in one statement and wrong in another is checked by the facts, not by a forbid.

expect context_dependent_binding <script>:1 | S1 is the first unqualified reference resolved by assumption; one boundary per unit (D-24)
expect dangling_reference events_log | S3: events_log is in staging and mart and neither is the default, so it is ambiguous (D-24)

@ 18 S1 default schema, no path known
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.kpi_rollup.region identity
value core.dim_store.country_code -> mart.kpi_rollup.country_code identity

@ 26 S2 unique name, no path known (D-24)
value staging.shipments.carrier_id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.carrier_id identity
value staging.shipments.id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.shipments aggregated
influence staging.shipments.carrier_id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.shipments

@ 36 S3 ambiguous name, no path known (D-24)
forbid value staging.events_log.kind -> mart.kpi_rollup.level | events_log is ambiguous with no path known: no edge from either table (D-24)
# mart.events_log.kind -> mart.kpi_rollup.level is right in S8, so S3's half of the rule is checked by the boundary above.

@ 51 S5 path order: staging before core
value staging.ledger.account -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity
value staging.ledger.amount -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue identity
filter staging.ledger.currency -> mart.kpi_rollup

@ 60 S6 falls through to the path's second schema
value core.dim_warehouse.region -> mart.kpi_rollup.region identity

@ 68 S7 a qualifier overrides the path
value core.ledger.account -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity
value core.ledger.balance -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue identity

@ 79 S8 a new path; unqualified target
value mart.events_log.kind -> mart.kpi_rollup.level identity
filter mart.events_log.rolled_up -> mart.kpi_rollup

@ 91 S9 after RESET: the default schema
value core.ledger.status -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity

@ 100 S10 quoted identifiers
value staging.LegacyFeed.CustomerID -> mart.FeedSummary.CustomerID identity
value staging.LegacyFeed.Amount -> mart.FeedSummary.Total identity
value staging.LegacyFeed.amount -> mart.FeedSummary.total identity
value staging.LegacyFeed.order -> mart.FeedSummary.order identity
value staging.LegacyFeed.Status Code -> mart.FeedSummary.Status Code identity
filter staging.LegacyFeed.user -> mart.FeedSummary
forbid value staging.LegacyFeed.amount -> mart.FeedSummary.Total | "Amount" and amount are different columns
forbid value staging.LegacyFeed.Amount -> mart.FeedSummary.total | "Total" and total are different columns

@ 109 S11 folding and quoted lower case
value staging.customers.country_code -> mart.kpi_rollup.region identity
value staging.customers.segment -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity

@ 117 S12 three-part names
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.channel identity
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.channel_mix.revenue identity
filter staging.orders.status -> mart.channel_mix

@ 126 S13 SELECT * into the same-shaped table
value core.ledger.id -> core.ledger.id identity
value core.ledger.account -> core.ledger.account identity
value core.ledger.balance -> core.ledger.balance identity
value core.ledger.status -> core.ledger.status identity
filter core.ledger.status -> core.ledger

@ 136 S14 t.* over a USING join
value staging.customers.full_name -> mart.top_customers.full_name identity
value staging.orders.customer_id -> mart.top_customers.customer_id identity
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.top_customers.revenue identity
forbid filter staging.customers.id -> mart.top_customers | USING is a join condition: structural (D-5)

@ 149 S15a FULL JOIN USING
value staging.orders.store_id, core.fct_order_line.store_id -> mart.sales_daily.store_id conditional
note The merged column is COALESCE(a.store_id, b.store_id): two columns (D-19).
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.sales_daily.gross_amount identity
value core.fct_order_line.net_amount -> mart.sales_daily.net_amount identity

@ 158 S15b RIGHT JOIN USING
value core.fct_order_line.store_id -> mart.sales_daily.store_id identity
repeat value core.fct_order_line.net_amount -> mart.sales_daily.net_amount identity
forbid value staging.orders.store_id -> mart.sales_daily.store_id identity | under RIGHT JOIN the merged column is the right input's

@ 168 S15c NATURAL JOIN
repeat value staging.ledger.account -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity
repeat value core.ledger.balance -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue identity
forbid filter staging.ledger.id -> mart.kpi_rollup | NATURAL's shared columns are the join condition: structural (D-5)

@ 177 S16 COLLATE
value staging.customers.segment -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment derived
note COLLATE stands between the column and the target: derived, as a cast is.
filter staging.customers.full_name -> mart.kpi_rollup
note ORDER BY full_name under LIMIT decides which rows land (D-9).
